/T (For two campuses, static routing needs a route statement at each router for the remote LAN, plus interface configuration. OSPF needs an OSPF process and network statements on each router. For five campuses, static routing requires multiple manually maintained routes and grows with the number of networks; OSPF advertises learned routes automatically. OSPF usually adapts faster and scales better, but adds protocol configuration and control traffic. Exact recovery time must be measured in the simulation; it depends on timers, topology and failure detection.)
