/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 71 0 R
/T (Traceroute sends probes with increasing TTL values. The first probe has TTL 1; the first router reduces it to zero and discards it, returning an ICMP Time Exceeded message. The next probe uses TTL 2 and reaches the second router before expiring. Repeating this process reveals each hop until the destination is reached. In IPv6, the corresponding message is ICMPv6 Time Exceeded.)
/E (Traceroute sends probes with increasing TTL values. The first probe has TTL 1; the first router reduces it to zero and discards it, returning an ICMP Time Exceeded message. The next probe uses TTL 2 and reaches the second router before expiring. Repeating this process reveals each hop until the destination is reached. In IPv6, the corresponding message is ICMPv6 Time Exceeded.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [23]
>>
