441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 72 0 R
/T (A 6in4 tunnel adds a 20-byte IPv4 outer header to the original IPv6 packet. For a 100-byte inner sensor packet, the tunnel carries 120 bytes before link-layer overhead: 20 bytes extra, which is a 20% increase relative to the original 100 bytes. Direct IPv6 avoids this tunnel overhead but requires IPv6 support throughout the path. Dual-stack allows IPv4 and IPv6 to operate together during migration, but requires managing both protocols. A practical city rollout can begin with dual-stack and use 6in4 tunnelling only where IPv6-native transport is not yet available.)
/E (A 6in4 tunnel adds a 20-byte IPv4 outer header to the original IPv6 packet. For a 100-byte inner sensor packet, the tunnel carries 120 bytes before link-layer overhead: 20 bytes extra, which is a 20% increase relative to the original 100 bytes. Direct IPv6 avoids this tunnel overhead but requires IPv6 support throughout the path. Dual-stack allows IPv4 and IPv6 to operate together during migration, but requires managing both protocols. A practical city rollout can begin with dual-stack and use 6in4 tunnelling only where IPv6-native transport is not yet available.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
