784 0 obj
<<
/Title (SDN is useful for a smart city because a central controller can apply consistent policies, manage traffic engineering and update forwarding rules across many switches. The trade-offs are controller availability, security, skills and deployment cost. A resilient controller design and secure control channel are important.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 713 0 R
/Next 785 0 R
>>
endobj
785 0 obj
<<
/Title (A 6in4 tunnel adds a 20-byte IPv4 outer header to the original IPv6 packet. For a 100-byte inner sensor packet, the tunnel carries 120 bytes before link-layer overhead: 20 bytes extra, which is a 20% increase relative to the original 100 bytes. Direct IPv6 avoids this tunnel overhead but requires IPv6 support throughout the path. Dual-stack allows IPv4 and IPv6 to operate together during migration, but requires managing both protocols. A practical city rollout can begin with dual-stack and use 6in4 tunnelling only where IPv6-native transport is not yet available.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 713 0 R
/Prev 784 0 R
>>
endobj
786 0 obj
<<
/Title (192.168.10.0/24 pool is almost fully allocated and the remaining 28 addresses cannot support the new 60-host hostel.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 647 0 R
/Prev 714 0 R
/Next 860 0 R
>>
endobj
787 0 obj
<<
/Title (E. Implement and validate \(2 marks\))
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 647 0 R
/Prev 861 0 R
/First 862 0 R
/Last 863 0 R
/Count -2
/Next 715 0 R
>>
endobj
788 0 obj
<<
/Title (The objective is achieved because the revised /23 allocation preserves the existing subnet addresses and provides an aligned /26 for the 60-host hostel. The new design costs more address space and may require a larger provider allocation and configuration updates. The original /24 remains preferable if no growth is expected and conserving address space is the main priority. For a growing campus, the /23 plan is more practical.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 715 0 R
/Next 789 0 R
>>
endobj
789 0 obj
<<
/Title (Final conclusion: VLSM uses address space efficiently, but growth must be planned. Expanding the contiguous allocation to /23 allows the new hostel subnet to be added without renumbering the existing networks.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 715 0 R
/Prev 788 0 R
>>
endobj
