/Title (In datagram switching, every packet is routed independently. Packets from the same file may take different paths because of congestion or routing changes; therefore, they may arrive out of order. The receiver uses sequence information in higher-layer protocols to reassemble them. In virtual-circuit switching, a logical path is established before data transfer and packets normally follow that path in sequence, although a failure can interrupt the circuit.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 777 0 R
>>
endobj
